Cryft platform contract examples: licences

This repository is under two licences, file by file. Each file's own licence is the first line of that file (its
SPDX-License-Identifier), and matches the licence of the contract it was adapted from. provenance.json lists every
Solidity file, its licence and its origin; NOTICE lists every original and upstream with its copyright.

  MIT (full text: LICENSE-MIT)
    contracts/01-upgradeable/Initializable.sol        adapted from Cryft's Initializable, itself based on
                                                      OpenZeppelin Contracts Upgradeable v4.9.6 (MIT)
    contracts/04-collectible-1155/CollectibleItems.sol adapted from Cryft's Giftables (MIT)

  Apache-2.0 (full text: LICENSE-APACHE, with Cryft Labs' patent notice)
    every other file: the other contracts, the Remix tests, the pytest suite and its Solidity support files, the tools,
    and the documentation

Portions of some files derive from OpenZeppelin Contracts v4.9.6 (MIT, Copyright (c) 2016-2023 zOS Global Limited
and contributors); those files say so in their headers, and NOTICE carries OpenZeppelin's licence. The ERC-1967 storage
slots and the ERC-1155 receiver interface follow the Ethereum standards, which are CC0-1.0.
